# The only vuln is in the standard library, so the fix is a `go` directive bump
# rather than a module upgrade.
#
# govulncheck reports GO-2024-2687 against `stdlib` with a fix in go1.21.9, and
# govulncheck-apply bumps the `go` directive from 1.21.0 to 1.21.9. The main
# module has no require directives, so go.mod is the only file touched.
#
# govulncheck takes the standard library version from the toolchain running the
# scan, not from the `go` directive, so the test sets GOTOOLCHAIN to go1.21.0;
# a current toolchain would already be past the fix and report nothing.

gotoolchain: go1.21.0
-- go.mod --
module example.com/foo

go 1.21.0
-- main.go --
package main

import "net/http"

func main() {
	http.Get("http://example.com/")
}
-- want_diff.txt --
diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index 9b981c3..d7e9510 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 module example.com/foo
 
-go 1.21.0
+go 1.21.9
-- want_report.md --
| Module | Advisory | Dependency | Fixed in | Reached from |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `.` | [GO-2024-2687](https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2024-2687 "HTTP/2 rapid reset can cause excessive work in net/http") | net/http@go1.21.0 → go1.21.9 | go1.21.9 | main.go:6:10 foo.main → http.Get |
